From c87b6505568ca3a42c81b998cd446742baaf7c59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:14:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 887/913] drivers: regulator: compute the level range without
 underflow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the supply exposes a full list of voltages whose first level above
the minimum constraint is already above the maximum constraint, the
retained range is empty. The "end = i - 1" and "end - start" expressions
were then evaluated on unsigned values that wrap around, and the only
guard was an assert, hence unchecked in release builds.

Break out of the second loop without touching "end", reject an empty
range by comparing the two indexes, and only then derive "end". Both
subtractions are now reached with a proven non-empty range, so neither
"i - 1" nor "end - start" can wrap around. An empty range returns
TEE_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, so the caller falls back to the default voltage
range as already done for incremental descriptions.

Coverity issue: CID 1200021: Overflowed constant in regulator_limit_levels

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 5398256a6ba0440e1bb1a6645f6149123192a725 drivers: regulator: compute the level range without underflow]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I46155feb75f1ae303534dad6111c65a5c725d895
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/597008
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/regulator/regulator.c | 16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/regulator/regulator.c b/core/drivers/regulator/regulator.c
index cd23d8200..6776360f4 100644
--- a/core/drivers/regulator/regulator.c
+++ b/core/drivers/regulator/regulator.c
@@ -256,14 +256,20 @@ static TEE_Result regulator_limit_levels(struct regulator *regulator,
 				start = i;
 				break;
 			}
-		/* Last level lower than maximum */
+		/* First level higher than the maximum, if any */
 		for (; i  <= last ; i++)
-			if ((*levels)[i] > regulator->max_uv) {
-				end = i - 1;
+			if ((*levels)[i] > regulator->max_uv)
 				break;
-			}
+
+		/* No supported level fits both constraints */
+		if (i == start)
+			return TEE_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+
+		/* Last level lower than maximum */
+		if (i <= last)
+			end = i - 1;
+
 		/* Expose only a subset of supported voltages by the supply */
-		assert(end >= start);
 		if (start > 0 && end != last) {
 			*levels = *levels + start;
 			(*desc)->num_levels = end - start + 1;
-- 
